<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1651) <span class="when">Oct 16, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>ACES 1.3 and 2.0 configs keep your settings.</b> Moving from ACES 1.2 to 1.3 (or back, or on to 2.0), a saved display and view keep their screen: 1.2&#8217;s &#8220;ACES&#8221; / &#8220;Rec.709&#8221; becomes 1.3&#8217;s &#8220;Rec.1886 Rec.709 - Display&#8221; / &#8220;ACES 1.0 - SDR Video&#8221;, for the window, the default view and each file&#8217;s own view.</li>
<li><b>Movies and stills decode correctly under the newer ACES configs.</b> They go in through &#8220;Output - Rec.709&#8221; and &#8220;Output - sRGB&#8221; as in ACES 1.2; configs without those spaces now get them, made from the config&#8217;s own ACES view. Before, the built-in config read a movie darker and tone-mapped it twice. A packaged review proxy made under these configs now declares the same space, so it opens as it was made.</li>
<li><b>The built-in config is now ACES 1.3.</b> With no config set (no $OCIO and nothing in Settings), Asobi uses the ACES 1.3 config built into OpenColorIO, the same as Kura&#8217;s aces_1.3, instead of ACES 2.0. Pictures look as they do under ACES 1.2, not 2.0&#8217;s slightly different rendering.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
